{
  "about": "Documented design systems a product can be built on. Each entry is a system its owner publishes and maintains, with its own rules, tokens and components. Packages, licenses and repositories were read from the npm registry on the date in `checked`; documentation addresses are the owners' published ones. Nothing here is a design system invented for one project. CSS token prefixes were read from the packages' own files on the same date. `limits` says what a brand may adjust and what stays fixed, from how each system is themed.",
  "checked": "2026-11-05",
  "categories": {
    "enterprise-product": "Complex web products used every day at work: forms, tables, settings, workflows",
    "data-dense": "Screens that must show a lot at once: dashboards, back offices, analytics, trading, admin",
    "commerce": "Selling, stores, merchants, checkout",
    "public-service": "Government and public services used by everyone, with strict accessibility and plain language",
    "editorial": "Reading first: news, magazines, publications, long text",
    "developer-tools": "Products for engineers: code, infrastructure, consoles",
    "consumer": "Apps for the general public, often mobile first",
    "japanese": "Built for Japanese text and Japanese users: CJK type, line height and density",
    "composable": "Unstyled or lightly styled parts meant to be themed into a product's own identity",
    "platform": "The native guidelines of an operating system"
  },
